  "semantic_evidence": [
    {
      "unit": "requested answer roles and fields",
      "status": "pass",
      "original_quote": "Rank the main contributors to spec 38.331",
      "finding": "The requested record identifies a company in an ordered ranking; companyName supplies that role. The original design CQ3 ranks companies by count, but the English does not request displayed count or an extra rank integer, so contributionCount is native ranking evidence rather than an imposed required answer field. Identity-only ranked names can answer unchanged English.",
      "query_clauses": [
        "MATCH (r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec {specNumber:'38.331'}), (t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)",
        "RETURN c.companyName AS companyName, count(DISTINCT r) AS contributionCount",
        "ORDER BY contributionCount DESC, companyName ASC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "unit": "population and source context",
      "status": "pass",
      "original_quote": "main contributors to spec 38.331",
      "finding": "Original indexed Final_report design explicitly includes the specific-Spec main-contributor sentence in CQ3 and binds CQ3 to Resolution/references/Phase1 Tdoc/Company/Spec. All retained frozen Resolution and Tdoc/Company identities and relevant relations are input-pinned. The participant population is companies with at least one such recorded path for Spec38.331; companies with no recorded contribution are not invented contributors. All captured editions of that spec remain eligible; no latest/release/status/physical approval restriction appears.",
      "query_clauses": [
        "MATCH (r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec {specNumber:'38.331'}), (t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)",
        "RETURN c.companyName AS companyName, count(DISTINCT r) AS contributionCount",
        "ORDER BY contributionCount DESC, companyName ASC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "unit": "filters and relationship meaning",
      "status": "pass",
      "original_quote": "contributors to spec 38.331",
      "finding": "The original indexed CQ3 required-term and answerability tables specifically define references→Tdoc→submittedBy and Spec modifies. This is recorded Resolution attribution through a cited Tdoc that modifies the named Spec, with submitted company roles. Count DESC in that exact CQ group identifies the ranking operation. The parenthetical RRC ownership does not introduce a legal/normative ownership entity into this documented benchmark path; no patent influence, adoption or exclusive ownership is asserted.",
      "query_clauses": [
        "MATCH (r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec {specNumber:'38.331'}), (t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)",
        "RETURN c.companyName AS companyName, count(DISTINCT r) AS contributionCount",
        "ORDER BY contributionCount DESC, companyName ASC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "unit": "counting unit and join multiplicity",
      "status": "pass",
      "original_quote": "contributors",
      "finding": "Resolution is the original CQ3 object, not Tdoc volume or final CR number. count(DISTINCT r) attributes each recorded Resolution once per company even when multiple cited Tdocs, co-submitted documents or duplicate spec-edition paths witness it. Multiple co-submitters can each receive recorded attribution according to the schema; this is not fractional/legal ownership. Whole unfiltered Resolution IDs, company canonical names and Tdoc IDs were checked unique/non-null, so document/entity unit correspondence is bounded explicitly.",
      "query_clauses": [
        "MATCH (r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec {specNumber:'38.331'}), (t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)",
        "RETURN c.companyName AS companyName, count(DISTINCT r) AS contributionCount",
        "ORDER BY contributionCount DESC, companyName ASC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "unit": "cardinality and completeness",
      "status": "pass",
      "original_quote": "main contributors",
      "finding": "The indexed design explicitly declares TopN default10 for CQ3, while saying parameterized limits can be adjusted; the unchanged question supplies no alternate limit. This is preserved original context, not sole reliance on the old LIMIT10. Native uncapped fullpool establishes complete eligible rank population; required returned extent is min(10,population). It is not an arbitrary universal ten-company scientific claim or an invented five-work-item slice.",
      "query_clauses": [
        "MATCH (r:Resolution)-[:REFERENCES]->(t:Tdoc)-[:MODIFIES]->(sp:Spec {specNumber:'38.331'}), (t)-[:SUBMITTED_BY]->(c:Company)",
        "RETURN c.companyName AS companyName, count(DISTINCT r) AS contributionCount",
        "ORDER BY contributionCount DESC, companyName ASC"
      ]
    },
    {
